Apple Pie Cyser (Makes One Gallon (Hopefully))

Adapted to One Gallon (Original Recipe: homebrewtalk.com/threads/apple-pie-cyser.436094/)

MeadTools Estimates:
OG: 1.095
FG: 0.998
ABV: 12.5%

Ingredients:

1 Gallon Apple Cider
1 Pound Wildflower Honey (13 oz for primary, 3 oz for secondary)
12 oz Brown Sugar
8 oz Apple Juice Concentrate
1 Teaspoon Apple Pie Spice
1 Cinnamon Stick
1/2 Packet Yeast (US-05/S-04)

Procedure:

1. Add cider, 13 oz honey, and brown sugar to 2 gallon fermenting bucket. Stir until combined and aerated.
2. Install airlock; store in a cool, dry place until airlock has less than 1 bubble per minute (original recipe says about 2.5 weeks, but likely longer).
3. Dissolve 3 oz honey into 2 cups warm water. Stir in apple juice concentrate. Add to 1 gallon carboy, alongside muslin bag containing spices.
4. Rack over from bucket into carboy. Keep cool and dark for another month.
5. Stabilize and fine. Allow to clear for 2-3 weeks. Rack into bottles.
6. Age for 6 months.
